  "worked_solution": "Let's simplify the expression using the properties of logical operation\n\n- First, we use that $X\u21d2Y\u2261\u00acX\u2228Y:$\n\n$$\nA\u2227(A\u21d2B)\u2261A\u2227(\u00acA\u2228B)\n$$\n\n- Then, we use the distributive law (disjunction over conjunction):\n\n$$\nA\u2227(\u00acA\u2228B)\u2261(A\u2227\u00acA)\u2228(A\u2227B)\n$$\n\n- Next,  we use the fact that the conjunction of a statement and its negation is a contradiction:\n\n$$\n(A\u2227\u00acA)\u2228(A\u2227B)\u2261c\u2228(A\u2227B)\n$$\n\n- Finally, we use the fact that the disjunction of a statement and a contradiction equals the original statement:\n\n$$\nc\u2228(A\u2227B)\u2261(A\u2227B)\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\nA\u2227(A\u21d2B)\u2261A\u2227B\n$$",
